1
00:00:03,060 --> 00:00:07,200
足迹交易法课程，第10单元。
The Footprint Course, Unit 10.

3
00:00:07,520 --> 00:00:09,320
这是30天挑战的第17天。
This is Challenge Day 17 of 30.

4
00:00:09,320 --> 00:00:15,440
接下来我们聚焦从亏损表现中恢复的技巧。
In the following slide, we are going to focus on the art of recovery from poor performance.

6
00:00:15,820 --> 00:00:20,020
重点是如何随时间培养恢复技能。
The focus will be on how to develop recovery skills over time.

7
00:00:46,090 --> 00:00:48,844
我分享这个的目的是，我会给你三个步骤分解的流程，帮你培养自己的恢复技能。
The purpose of me going through this is,

8
00:00:48,844 --> 00:00:52,287
I’m going to give you three step-by-step processes

9
00:00:52,287 --> 00:00:55,386
on how you can develop your own recovery skills.

10
00:00:55,590 --> 00:01:00,350
把这些当作训练。这些是我给你的训练，就像乔丹·斯皮思有他的训练一样。
Think of this as drills. These are the drills I’m giving you, just like Jordan Spieth has drills.

12
00:01:00,710 --> 00:01:03,620
这是你的训练套路，你得去练习，如果你想提升恢复能力。第一步，
This is your drill set that you have to go practice

13
00:01:03,620 --> 00:01:05,736
if you want to become better at recovery.

14
00:01:05,736 --> 00:01:06,529
The first one,

15
00:01:06,670 --> 00:01:08,470
你必须学会情绪控制。
you have to learn emotional control.

16
00:01:08,870 --> 00:01:13,341
想提升恢复能力，唯一的路就是情绪控制。
The only way you’re ever going to become better at recovery is emotional control.

17
00:01:13,341 --> 00:01:17,870
首先，你要相信自己能恢复。
Now, the first thing to do is to understand that you *can* recover.

19
00:01:18,170 --> 00:01:19,610
多数人不这么认为。
Most people don’t think you can.

20
00:01:19,890 --> 00:01:22,770
多数人一旦亏损，就接受亏损，结束交易，然后继续。所以，
Most people, the minute they take the loss,

21
00:01:22,770 --> 00:01:26,010
they accept the loss and call it a day,

22
00:01:26,010 --> 00:01:27,810
and they move on. So,

23
00:01:28,070 --> 00:01:31,604
不承认为自己能恢复，这是你要跨过的一步。
failing to acknowledge that you can recover, that’s one step you need to get over.

24
00:01:31,604 --> 00:01:32,929
说到情绪控制，
Now, in terms of emotional control,

25
00:01:35,750 --> 00:01:38,809
一旦亏了大笔钱，你快要崩溃了。你需要暂时离开。
the minute you’ve lost a big chunk of money, you’re close to stopping. You need to walk away.

28
00:01:41,950 --> 00:01:45,890
你得有勇气站起来，暂时离开。
You need to have that strength to stand up and walk away.

30
00:01:46,570 --> 00:01:51,110
休息5分钟，或者15分钟。因为你会发现，
Take that five minutes, take that 15 minutes. Because what you will notice is

31
00:01:51,110 --> 00:01:54,451
如果不离开，你往往会亏损扩大。
That very often, if you do not walk away, you're going to end up digging that deep.

32
00:01:54,451 --> 00:01:57,989
你会让亏损的洞挖得更深。你会亏得更多，
You're going to end up digging that hole a lot deeper. You're going to end up losing more,

34
00:01:58,070 --> 00:02:00,372
还会陷入负面的心理状态。
but you're also going to end up being in a mental negative state.

35
00:02:00,372 --> 00:02:01,966
就算你坐在那里，什么都不做，
By sitting there, even if you don't do anything,

36
00:02:04,269 --> 00:02:10,030
下次需要恢复时，第一步：站起来，离开15分钟。
The next time you need to recover, step number one: get up and walk away for 15 minutes.

37
00:02:03,383 --> 00:02:04,268
从当前的困境中走出来。
that you're currently stuck in.

39
00:02:10,410 --> 00:02:18,142
在这15分钟里，在脑海中回顾，诚实面对亏损发生的真正原因。
Go through, in those 15 minutes, in your head, the honest reasons why what happened happened.

41
00:02:18,142 --> 00:02:24,328
你会发现，90%的情况，原因都在你的控制范围内。
You're going to find, 90% of the time, they were in your control.

44
00:02:24,330 --> 00:02:26,757
不管亏损多大，可能你出手太慢。
Whether it was a big loss, maybe you moved too slow.

45
00:02:26,757 --> 00:02:32,022
可能你因推特上有人喊单就进场，不管什么原因——写下来，记在纸上，承担责任。
Maybe you kind of got into a trade because some guy on Twitter said to get into a trade, whatever it may be—

46
00:02:32,022 --> 00:02:34,768
write it down, put it on a piece of paper, take ownership.

50
00:02:35,210 --> 00:02:39,369
因为一旦承担责任，不管是什么导致你亏损，你就会放下这个包袱。
Because once you take ownership of that, whatever caused you to take a big loss,

51
00:02:39,369 --> 00:02:41,310
you're going to let go of it.

52
00:02:41,311 --> 00:02:43,807
就好像我对你说：
It’s almost like if I said to you:

53
00:02:46,490 --> 00:02:48,630
这是你能控制的事情。
it happened with something that’s in your control.

54
00:02:48,630 --> 00:02:53,650
承认自己能控制，就能避免下次重复。
By acknowledging that it’s in your control, that means you can avoid doing it next time.

56
00:02:53,650 --> 00:02:57,370
突然，你会感觉肩上的重担卸下了。
All of a sudden, you're going to feel that burden on your shoulders lift off.

58
00:02:57,910 --> 00:02:59,412
这就是我们要做的。
That’s why we do it.

59
00:02:59,412 --> 00:03:03,169
所以第一步：暂时离开，接受亏损，承担它。
That’s why step one: we walk away. We accept the loss. We take it.

60
00:03:03,250 --> 00:03:06,710
对自己说：完事了，现在得往前看。
We say to ourselves: it’s done. Now I need to move on.

61
00:03:06,790 --> 00:03:10,652
现在得回到交易心态，继续前进。
Now I need to get back into that mental state and move on.

62
00:03:10,652 --> 00:03:13,029
职业高尔夫球手就很擅长这点。
That’s where professional golfers are so good.

63
00:03:13,030 --> 00:03:17,770
他们打一杆差球，6-7分钟后，就重新开始。
They can hit one bad shot and, literally six or seven minutes later, they’re back to square one.

65
00:03:17,810 --> 00:03:23,410
他们只关注当下，不纠结过去或未来。
All they focus on is not what has been or what will become. They focus on what is the now.

67
00:03:23,850 --> 00:03:26,390
这就是第一步的关键：情绪控制。
And that’s the key to step number one: emotional control.

68
00:03:26,870 --> 00:03:31,450
第二步是自信强化。很多人会说‘我有自信，我信任自己’，
Step number two is self-belief. Now, a lot of people say, 'Yes, I’ve got self-belief. I believe,'

70
00:03:31,650 --> 00:03:33,490
很多人会说‘我有自信，我信任自己’，
but that’s not enough.

71
00:03:33,490 --> 00:03:38,274
但这还不够。
So I’m going to give you another process to develop your self-belief.

72
00:03:38,274 --> 00:03:40,850
我会给你一个方法来培养自信。
And it’s called an opportunity sheet.

73
00:03:40,950 --> 00:03:43,555
它叫机会清单。每天交易结束后，我会在复盘时记录当天的所有机会。
At the end of every single day, after my trading day,

74
00:03:43,555 --> 00:03:48,055
what I do is I write down in my debrief all the opportunities that were there in a day

75
00:03:48,055 --> 00:03:48,765
across whatever markets.

76
00:03:48,810 --> 00:03:54,727
无论在哪个市场。我发现，通常在正常交易日里，
What I’ve tended to find is that, in general, on average, in a normal trading day,

77
00:03:54,727 --> 00:03:59,947
all things being equal, you’re looking at between five and eight unique tradable opportunities.

79
00:04:00,290 --> 00:04:02,339
平均能找到5到8个可交易的机会。这些是我能执行并赚钱的机会，
Opportunities I could have executed and made good money

80
00:04:02,339 --> 00:04:05,526
because I understand the setup and the management and all that sort of thing.

82
00:04:07,420 --> 00:04:11,740
因为我懂入场形态和交易管理。如果你在周末看交易记录或复盘，
If you look at your trading sheet at the end of the week—or your debriefs—

83
00:04:11,740 --> 00:04:14,440
and you see that over the course of a week,

84
00:04:14,440 --> 00:04:16,870
其实有40个机会能让你赚钱。
there were 40 opportunities where you could have made money.

86
00:04:18,050 --> 00:04:20,350
先停下来想想这个数字。
Just think about that for a second.

87
00:04:20,490 --> 00:04:27,790
当你有这份机会清单时，我知道自己确实亏了钱。
Because the minute you have this opportunity sheet, I know full well that, yes, I’ve lost money.

89
00:04:27,990 --> 00:04:34,890
但猜怎么着？今天平均会有5到8个新机会。
But guess what? I know on average, there’s going to be five to eight unique opportunities today.

91
00:04:35,070 --> 00:04:36,630
可能我今天只抓住了2个。
So guess what? I may only have had two.

92
00:04:36,730 --> 00:04:40,190
那意味着今天还有3到5个机会在等我。
That means I'm likely to see three to five more opportunities.

94
00:04:40,790 --> 00:04:41,710
何必如此焦虑呢？
What's all the fuss about?

95
00:04:41,770 --> 00:04:43,198
何必如此沮丧呢？
Why am I so upset?

96
00:04:43,198 --> 00:04:46,910
因为猜怎么着？我有机会把钱赚回来。
Because guess what? I'm going to have the opportunity to get it back.

97
00:04:46,910 --> 00:04:48,909
这就是机会清单的关键。
That's the key to the opportunity sheet.

98
00:04:51,977 --> 00:04:58,248
如果你以正确心态执行，就能把钱赚回来。
that if you were to execute in the right frame of mind, you will get that money back.

100
00:04:58,248 --> 00:05:00,687
这就是机会清单的关键。
That's the key to the opportunity sheet.

101
00:05:00,990 --> 00:05:01,970
本周就试试看。
Try it out this week.

102
00:05:02,390 --> 00:05:08,290
最后一点：你需要现实策略。这包括仓位管理。
The last one: you need a realistic approach. This includes clip management.

103
00:05:08,410 --> 00:05:15,596
对我来说，亏损后恢复时，我会先减仓。为什么？
For me, in general, when I take a big hit and need to recover, I start slow. Why?

105
00:05:15,596 --> 00:05:19,189
没必要测试我的情绪承受力。
There is no point in testing my emotional ability.

107
00:05:19,350 --> 00:05:23,930
我知道自己亏损时会怎么反应。所以我会这样做：
I know how I respond when I'm far down. So what I tend to do,

108
00:05:24,390 --> 00:05:30,103
如果我习惯每笔交易风险$1,000，现在只会风险$250。
if I'm used to risking, say, $1,000 per trade, I'm now going to risk $250 per trade.

110
00:05:32,470 --> 00:05:34,590
我会降低每笔交易的风险金额。
I'm going to reduce the amount I risk per trade.

111
00:05:34,710 --> 00:05:37,070
为什么？因为我的目标要现实。
Why? My objective needs to be realistic.

112
00:05:37,070 --> 00:05:41,790
现实点说，第一笔交易我只需要盈利。
Realistically, all I need to do on that first trade is make a winner.

113
00:05:42,110 --> 00:05:47,730
仅此而已。我还要像什么都没发生一样执行第一笔交易。
That's all. I also need to execute that first trade as if nothing else had happened.

115
00:05:47,810 --> 00:05:50,368
换句话说，像重新开始一样。
In other words, as though it was a clean slate.

116
00:05:50,368 --> 00:05:55,228
但很多交易者会用相同的方式和风险金额继续交易。
What tends to happen is traders tend to execute in the same manner with the same amount of risk.

118
00:05:55,710 --> 00:06:01,130
情绪会迅速爆发，尤其是立刻又亏损的时候。
That emotion quickly boils up, particularly if they go offsides instantly.

119
00:06:01,210 --> 00:06:02,670
所以我会减少仓位。
So I reduce the clip.

120
00:06:03,010 --> 00:06:09,565
比如，如果我今天亏了$10,000，我会分步骤来。
I then write out, if I'm, say, $10,000 down on the day, I go right out, you do the increments.

122
00:06:09,565 --> 00:06:12,978
我会对自己说：“好的，任务就是”我要一次赚回一个仓位——$1,000，$1,000，$2,000。
And I say to myself, 'Well, yes, the job,'

123
00:06:12,978 --> 00:06:17,528
I need to get one of these clips back at a time—

124
00:06:17,528 --> 00:06:20,182
$1,000, $1,000, $2,000.

125
00:06:17,810 --> 00:06:21,370
只需要重复5次。猜怎么着？我就回本了。
And all I’ve got to do is five times. Then, guess what? I’m back at zero.

126
00:06:21,530 --> 00:06:25,130
所以我把它拆解，给自己设一个小目标这样我就不会陷入过去或未来的思绪里
So I break it down, I create a little gain for myself,

127
00:06:25,130 --> 00:06:30,230
a little target so that I don’t get caught thinking about the past or the future.

129
00:06:30,430 --> 00:06:37,630
我只专注当下，每一笔交易。好，这就是分步流程
All I focus on is the now, each individual shot. Okay, guys, that’s the step-by-step process

131
00:06:37,630 --> 00:06:41,290
要提升恢复技能
to become better at developing the skill of recovery.

132
00:06:41,590 --> 00:06:46,010
职业高尔夫球手和职业交易者，道理完全相同
It’s no different for a professional golfer than it is for a professional trader.
